  "result": "**Final verdict: `OK`** (first gate run, 1 of 6 budgeted used).\n\n**Body** — the contract's one element, over the formals and the two claimed atoms:\n\n```lean\ndef alongHeading : Term :=\n  .add (.mul (.measure \"kin_velocity\" [aU, .lit \"x\"]) (.measure \"kin_heading\" [aU, .lit \"x\"]))\n       (.mul (.measure \"kin_velocity\" [aU, .lit \"y\"]) (.measure \"kin_heading\" [aU, .lit \"y\"]))\n\ndef body : Formula := .cmp alongHeading .le (.neg pReverseSpeedTolerance)\n```\n\nThe component along the direction the body points is the inner product with `kin.heading`, which Core reads normalised, so the sum of products is the signed speed in m/s; \"at most the negative of the reverse speed tolerance\" is `.le (.neg …)`. No region, device, signal or control-state atom enters it, and neither `kin.speed` nor `kin.gear` does.\n\n**Witnesses** — one instance (`reverse_speed_tolerance` 0.30 m/s), track 1 a motor vehicle heading north over three 1 s observations, a parking-bay region that nothing reads: `holds` has velocity (0, −1.5) m/s so the component is −1.5; `fails` drives forward at +1.5; `blind` is the reversing trace with `kin.velocity` masked, the heading still read, so the masked atom is the one that decides. No window is needed — the concept speaks about the observation only.\n\n**Readings chosen:** none, so `narrowings := []`. The contract fixes the quantity, the sense of the bound and the instant; the only unstated thing is how the component is formed from the two vector atoms, and the surface offers exactly one way (the `\"x\"`/`\"y\"` selectors), which is a consequence of the language, not a choice among meanings. Reasoning is in both file headers and in `/local-scratch2/sma407/scratch_core/launch/remote/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/results/demo22-1109-0108/iter-002/code/concept__drv_motion_reverse_travel/task_result.md`.",
